<section class="lesson-card" id="worked-example">
<h2>5. Worked examples: choosing the correct model</h2>
<p>A steel quality team studies pipe failures and surface defects.</p>
<div class="grid-3"><div class="concept-card">
<h3>Question A: exactly 2 failures in 20 pipes</h3>
<p>Suppose each pipe has a 10% failure probability.</p>
<div class="formula">P(X=2)=
  <span class="fraction"><span>20!</span><span>2!18!</span></span>
  (0.10)<sup>2</sup>(0.90)<sup>18</sup></div>
<p><strong>≈ 0.2852, or 28.5%</strong></p>
<p class="small">This is Binomial because there are 20 fixed pass/fail trials.</p>
</div>
<div class="concept-card">
<h3>Question B: exactly 3 defects in 100 m</h3>
<p>Here μ = 2 and x = 3.</p>
<div class="formula">P(X=3)=<span class="fraction"><span>e<sup>−2</sup>2<sup>3</sup></span><span>3!</span></span></div>
<p>= (0.1353 × 8) ÷ 6</p>
<p><strong>= 0.1804, or about 18.0%</strong></p>
<p class="small">Interpretation: in repeated 100 m sections, roughly 18% would contain exactly three defects under this model.</p>
</div>
<div class="concept-card">
<h3>Question C: travel more than 75 m with no defect</h3>
<p>Convert the rate: λ = 2/100 = 0.02 defect per metre.</p>
<div class="formula">P(T&gt;75)=e<sup>−0.02×75</sup></div>
<p>= e<sup>−1.5</sup></p>
<p><strong>= 0.2231, or about 22.3%</strong></p>
<p class="small">Interpretation: there is about a 22% chance the next 75 m contains no defect.</p>
</div>
</div>
<h3>Try the live probability calculator</h3>
<div class="controls">
<div class="control"><label for="calcRate">Rate per base unit</label><input id="calcRate" min="0.0001" step="0.1" type="number" value="2"/></div>
<div class="control"><label for="calcExposure">Exposure in base units</label><input id="calcExposure" min="0" step="0.1" type="number" value="1"/></div>
<div class="control"><label for="calcCount">Exact count x</label><input id="calcCount" min="0" step="1" type="number" value="3"/></div>
</div>
<div class="button-row">
<button class="btn" id="calculateBtn" type="button">Calculate both views</button>
<button class="btn secondary" id="resetCalcBtn" type="button">Reset calculator</button>
</div>
<div aria-live="polite" class="callout" id="calcMessage">Enter a rate, exposure, and count, then calculate.</div>
</section>
